{"step_index":1402,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T22:06:27Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T06:06:27+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T06:06:28+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T06:06:27+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T06:06:28+08:00\nShowing lines 1-19 of 19\n1: 1. For every changes Determine if a patch is a Major if so then must add a new subsequent patch entry following the previous patch number in `HISTORY.md`, For non-major patches, add the new changes below the current patch entry add why. Do not revise, replace, or update any of the existing patch details.\r\n2: 2. Do not build the APK. I will build it myself. YOU ARE PROHIBITED FROM TOUCHING/MODIFYING THE UNCODE ORIGINAL FILES OTHER THAN THE UI\r\n3: 3. Every update or proposed change must include a verification plan if the app works exactly as intended in the implementation_plan.md artifact across all Identify every file, class, component, or system behavior that directly or indirectly depends on the change, then specify how to verify that the app still works across those affected areas on devices. The verification must cover the changed file(s), their known dependents/callers, and any critical flow that could be affected and how do i verify those supposed flow or action still is working or is working.\r\n4: 4. SIREN HomeProxy is ONLY VIEWABLE; if YOU want to update it ask me anything explain why and what needs to be done\r\n5: 5. Always plan first after investigation use implementation plan(can always be edited regardless of any rule(any updates regarding implementation plan only negates rule 1)) is only for planning (not result of implementation)\r\n6: 6. You are not allowed to make any changes in any ocasions not until you ask me first plainly in text or if i clicked proceed with implementation plan.\r\n7: 7. **MANDATORY INVESTIGATION, RESEARCH & OPTIMIZATION:** For every requested code change, investigate the existing codebase and perform live web research relevant to the exact technologies, components, and problems involved before finalizing implementation decisions. Cross-reference the research with the existing implementation to identify\n<truncated 2550 bytes>\nf neither root access nor relevant Custom ROM functions are available, use standard ADB capabilities. You can even force stop/kill the app, Clear Logs at system or at kernel level if you want to see the issues further, basically anything you need to purge whatever issue it is.\r\n14: 12. **CRITICAL/SYSTEM FILE & LOG BACKUP:** When modifying, replacing, or deleting any system or critical OS file (local or on-device via ADB/root), create a timestamped backup directory at `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\` and follow this exact two-stage sequence:\r\n15:    - **Pre-Modification Target File Backup (BEFORE touching live files):**\r\n16:      - *Local Files:* Copy the untouched original file(s) into `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`, preserving the full relative directory structure to prevent filename collisions.\r\n17:      - *Android/ADB Files (under Rule 11):* Create an on-device backup in the same directory (`cp -a <file> <file>.bak`) to preserve exact UID/GID ownership, permissions, and SELinux contexts (`ls -Z`), AND pull a copy with its recorded `stat`/`ls -lZ` metadata to `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`.\r\n18:      - *Verification:* Verify that the target file backups exist and have a non-zero byte size matching the originals before modifying live system files. If the backup fails, abort immediately.\r\n19:    - **Post-Implementation Log Archival (ONLY AFTER executing the `implementation_plan.md` successfully):** Do not pre-backup session logs or plans. Once the implementation is completed and verified, copy the final `implementation_plan.md` and `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl` in full from the active session directory (`C:\\Users\\Admin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\<ACTIVE_SESSION_ID>\\`) into the same `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\` folder, along with a snippet of `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript_full.jsonl` saved as `transcript_full_snippet.jsonl` containing only the trailing entries for the completed task/turn. Verify these log files are non-zero before concluding the task.\n(no newline at end of file)","truncated_fields":["content"]}
