{"step_index":1414,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T22:09:21Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T06:09:21+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T06:09:33+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T06:09:21+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T06:09:33+08:00\nThe search for \"Antigravity IDE move or export conversation .gemini antigravity conversations db brain directory\" returned the following summary:\nIn the **Antigravity IDE** (and the broader Gemini Antigravity agent ecosystem), conversation history, context logs, and metadata are split across two primary layers: **human-readable brain artifacts/transcripts** and **internal SQLite/database indexes**[1][2]. \n\nDepending on whether you are trying to **move/migrate** your conversations between directories/versions (like upgrading to Antigravity IDE 2.0+) or **export** them into readable files, here is how the directory structure works and how to handle them.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Where Antigravity Stores Conversations & Brain Data\nAntigravity stores its operational data in two primary locations on your system (depending on your OS, typically Windows `%USERPROFILE%` / `%APPDATA%`[1] or macOS `~/.gemini/` and `~/Library/Application Support/`):\n\n* **The Brain / Artifact Directory (`~/.gemini/antigravity/brain/` or `~/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/`)**\n  * Contains folders named after individual conversation UUIDs[3][4].\n  * Inside each UUID folder, you will find raw execution logs (`transcript.jsonl`), scratch spaces, subagent trees, and generated files (`task.md`, implementation plans, code diff snapshots)[5][6].\n* **The Conversation Databases (`~/.gemini/antigravity/conversations/` or SQLite stores)**\n  * Contains `.db` files per conversation that track token metrics, model mappings, and transaction metadata[7].\n* **The IDE UI State Database (`%APPDATA%\\antigravity\\User\\globalStorage\\state.vscdb` or `antigravity-ide`)**\n  * An internal VS Code-style state database that maps what shows up in your sidebar history list (`trajectorySummaries`)[1][8].\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Export Conversations\nBecause Antigravity heavily relies on internal database structures and JSONL transcripts r\n<truncated 3704 bytes>\nf9hFdj6KQ6ZeWDT20X_pUrx528PmZXZKGhlA==)\n[7] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFr-rNy-wn1wI0kPRSCCujJToebL2C3_0wpT8grVh_r70a7xUqTUqkvUt4QEV1p-DldQp918FAslWr2OPRl3ZpMicmwyNvCXITYBb5S1av4ZhhJCyZo0z0Ij3wrTLe58iXOAjLpKxVDnvK5Uw==)\n[8] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF5TDt6kumSqasDyR4Cb-3UulV1HvXSDwCpPdv18_8QlR8GRfpIkKunWaSfPyQVovC3DLEcVAF_O3Z0zgv6ygPs3caOWwe9nXjwTsv2v3ffCiv_e6m0umH_4NMHsOMxYxOWUUqbx50xNxnOmAzaDcOKE5qSDXROd2ObXTZtNVQ7-4jkW30RTjG19lvRFo77-xSiV29_9ay-mBZoQryOiHHpkqcLjm21yPT-1Gogm6EdP8iQDzp3kzpwyOSUbHAfQSf6fb5L5qkdxrk=)\n[9] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHqUhq9oxqGrFL_bPzLkQ3JJjiYFmFwzi8h1A3ysSedW29TLl-k07wzFL7mwPBZx-4rVAb-qcnDeziSIkMcCgpYhMk6thL_1zq0cAXgxTgP6A1vJ-qy9c8eh0_nuvrEf33xDwWpeJZQVg2UTfQKgDY3i4g4PFgj)\n[10] [open-vsx.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEE1nNK_6FupdUwuOeZRcWnxDfnOjRQ4KkeF9MEf1-Qok4TVFqYQL5gzsdRaVAlxmvxYYybIFu5p27IczUSIcG9JAGMuYbIdUb16NMgA9RzFTnDaK8-GEc2ttoCJ3x7DJwWRkOz7dVjrAqc2-JvrNVyDlke)\n[11] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH7Ms1-_TthjvgDFYtuwIRXltr1ZrvcfDdKCwQHdkfJH1PVD6ccXFv4AV-Up8Z0MYzZHLetyUMEbLImm7rkOCAUJcvSdBgTQqTP3BEmi2wrgmfahiUV3MJnAvyTk5fer4zMIYvPCrbQYoq04opBK-zpaNfy6W5yGPZePBBffKtuIW-drEXp0gaXwKpL1XMoo5JPkWvIeA==)\n[12] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6vW1KThW9O-YasfJvZUZozD7K7_4VKcjehR9-t1NJRB129ERX5KYNHoVHeSizu-sl_I8rHhcm6K-rzS0CcPuaBwSkujiQ5PzJdpm7btbKOyQVIZa90bW20Fyrxi1di-sdkRTmzIHOMRcbu52bPNHjug==)\n[13] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF7U3V8EL9mZHVmeEuJ9WvWJWD3om